z5e = z3x (the incumbent) + SYM_RELAY (new switch, ledgered; Cfg.SYM_RELAY; Baby.symRelay, one hook after report()
with K 18). A rat merges the symmetry masks squeaked last round (SQ_SYM) into its own, and every SYM_GOSSIP_EVERY (3)
rounds squeaks its mask when it is sharper than the shared one, an ally is within d2 16 and no seen cat can hear it.
It runs after report(), so it never takes report()'s squeak (the engine allows one a turn and refuses the second).
A king that hears it merges it (King's SQ_SYM case) and writes the shared mask.

Evidence (local dumps with indicators, scratch symres.py and symres2.py in ~/diag26b; z1z and z3x vs araid and abrk,
seed 0): the king's mask stays ambiguous for most of the game on FreeTheCheese (unique at r584-1807), rift
(r826-841), clockwisdom (r484, r712 or never) and TheHeist (never), while 4-20 of our rats each knew it long before
(the first at r88-162 on FreeTheCheese, r138-157 on clockwisdom, r300-487 on rift). The rushers that cross the
midline see the twins and resolve it, then never come home to tell it, and the 12 rushers each walk to the nearest
live mirror spot: on clockwisdom the HOR spot (56,49) or (2,9) lies in a dirt corner they cannot reach. Rats tell the
king only within d2 16 (report()), and the s4k arm with SYM_GOSSIP (2026-10-28) was never scored. Panel cells on
those maps: clockwisdom (sets 1, 2, 4), FreeTheCheese (set 3, twice), TheHeist (sets 1, 2, 3), rift (set 3).

